---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="hadi's site">
  <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">hi, i'm hadi</h1>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    infosec engineer passionate about linux/nixos, blockchains, osint & foss.
    hacking with go, exploring open tech, and contributing whenever i can!
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">projects</h2>
  <p class="mb-3 leading-relaxed">
    i love building things myself, from scratch, just to understand how they
    really work. a few i'm working on:
  </p>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 leading-relaxed lowercase">
    <li>
      <a
        href="https://github.com/anotherhadi/default-creds"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">default-creds</a
      >: Default Creds is a centralized, community-driven repository of
      factory-set credentials. Designed for pentesters and security researchers,
      it helps identify weak access points during engagement phases or audit
      internal infrastructure before they become a security liability.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a
        href="https://github.com/anotherhadi/spilltea"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">spilltea</a
      >: A minimal, terminal-based HTTP(S) proxy for pentesters and CTF players.
      Think Burp Suite or Caido, but entirely in your terminal.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a
        href="https://github.com/anotherhadi/usbguard-tui"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">usbguard-tui</a
      >: a TUI to manage USBGuard device policies without touching a config
      file.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
    there's plenty more on <a
      href="https://github.com/anotherhadi"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer">github</a
    >, also mirrored on <a
      href="https://git.hadi.icu"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer">gitea</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">blog</h2>
  <p class="leading-relaxed">
    i write about privacy, infosec and osint on
    <a
      href="https://medium.com/@anotherhadi"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer">my blog on medium</a
    > and i also keep a pile of cybersecurity cheatsheets, in
    <a
      href="https://github.com/anotherhadi/sec-notes"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer">sec-notes</a
    >.
  </p>

  <p class="mt-8 leading-relaxed text-subtext">
    if you want to support what i do, there's <a href="/donate"
      >my lightning address</a
    >.
  </p>
</Layout>
